WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.060
A gorilla stands beside a giant
ape of exactly the same shape,

2
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.180
ten times as tall.

3
00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:10.030
Every length is ten
times bigger: arms, legs,

4
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.090
even the width of each bone.

5
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:15.730
So shouldn't the giant simply
be ten times as strong?

6
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.780
Yet its legs would snap.

7
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.260
Why would a perfect
copy, just bigger, fail?

8
00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:23.960
In this mission, you'll
meet similar shapes:

9
00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:28.560
equal angles, and every length
multiplied by the same scale factor.

10
00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:32.750
You'll find out what happens to areas
and volumes when every length is scaled

11
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:33.570
up.

12
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:38.570
And you'll use a model: a bone's strength
depends on its cross-sectional area,

13
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.820
and weight depends on volume.

14
00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.750
Your mission: explain why the
giant ape's legs would snap.
